# A season word that is also a common verb. "fall [...] (intransitive) To
# drop or descend" is the first verb sense; "fall [...] (US) Autumn" is a noun
# sense (Wiktionary, s.v. "fall"). Such a word reads as the season only after a
# preposition or an article or "this", "next" or "last" before it, before a
# year or the solar event, with a part of the period ("late fall"), or alone.
fall
